WEBVTT

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.500
Those Snow

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.500
White Notes

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.280
Episode 3
Sudden Downpour

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.950
Shuri.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.280
Morning.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.910
Oh, Yui-chan!

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.450
I'm amazed you don't get sick
of listening to that all the time.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.030
Well, this is the only lead I have.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:46.280
Plus, listening to it gets me pumped
to practice the shamisen.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.290
I wouldn't mind hanging out with
you during practice sometimes.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.730
Thank you!

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:57.180
I said "sometimes"! Sometimes!
You're so annoying!

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.290
That's Sawamura-kun.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.900
You know, the guy who helped me put
the shamisen together the other day.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.010
What is it?

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.920
Oh, no, nothing.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.690
E-Excuse me! Sawamura-kun!

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.400
Thank you for before.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.290
Sure. No problem.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.700
Hold it.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.000
This girl is in the Tsugaru Shamisen
Appreciation Club all by herself.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.560
Have you picked a club yet? Want to join?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.920
Y-Yui-chan?!

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.040
Why don't you join it?

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.040
Me? I'm not interested.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.000
Then, talk to me when you are.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.740
What's with that guy?!

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.830
He's a loner in your class, isn't he?!

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.720
I don't think I've seen him talk to anyone...

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.560
Exactly!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.000
Hey, Shuri!

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.670
Kaito.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.120
Who was that guy just now?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.690
If he's causing you trouble...

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.400
I-I'm fine. Nothing happened.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.400
What is it? Just tell me.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.020
Everything's fine!

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.680
So she says.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.000
H-Huh?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.200
What do ya wanna do today?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.570
Hm... How about karaoke?

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.760
<i>Why does she want to play Tsugaru shamisen?</i>

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.590
Grandma: A Song From Her Memories

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.060
<i>Grandma, what comes next?</i>

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.720
<i>Oh, I don't remember.</i>

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.920
<i>I'm sorry, Shuri.</i>

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.460
Hey! Maeda!

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.010
Recess is over! Stop playing
with your cell phone.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.520
Oh, I... I'm sorry.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.090
What are you doing? Texting?

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:03.800
I'm confiscating this!

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.310
Grandma: A Song From Her Memories

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:16.880
Wh-What is this?

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.870
Don't laugh!

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.110
I'll hang on to this for now.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.230
You're coming to the faculty room
with me after class!

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.160
<i>How...</i>

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.840
<i>That phrase just now...</i>

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.470
<i>That was Gramps' piece, "Shungyou (Spring Dawn)."</i>

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.460
I knew it.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.720
It's him, no doubt about it.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.820
Ah, this feeling of superiority,
being the only one who knows...

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.150
Uh-oh. This woman looks like trouble.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.790
You could at least knock.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.020
The door was wide open.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.150
Anyway, I'm looking for Shuri.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.480
I feel like she's been
avoiding me for a while now.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.540
I remembered she usually comes
here to play shamisen at lunch...

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.690
Are you stupid?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.160
She isn't avoiding you. She hates you!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:18.080
The reason Shuri doesn't like men is
because you bullied her when she was little!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.170
Now you're a second-year
and Shuri's your junior,

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.940
you say she's an "old friend" and
"like a little sister" to cozy up to her.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.040
It's absurd!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.840
It's obvious you have a crush on Shuri.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.820
Oh, well, it's not like I've tried to hide it.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:36.530
And the "old friend" and "little sister"
stuff... That's how I see you, too.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.800
Ludicrous.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.540
Huh?

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.160
<i>But how, Maeda Shuri?</i>

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.400
<i>How do you know Gramps'...</i>

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.330
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.830
Lost...

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.180
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.580
Lost...

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.040
<i>Where's the faculty room?</i>

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.210
Faculty Room

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.440
Thank you.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.970
<i>I'm so glad he gave it back.</i>

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.050
<i>Grandma doesn't sing it for me anymore.</i>

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:12.190
There you are!

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.180
I've been looking for you everywhere.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.320
Huh? Looking for me?! Wh-Why?!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.560
What happened to that thing
you were listening to before?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.160
You mean my cell phone? He gave it back.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.620
No, not that.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.080
That phrase of music. Where did
you hear it? How do you know it?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.520
W-Wait, does that mean...

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.520
Sawamura-kun, you know it, too?

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.620
I'm not completely certain, but... probably.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.550
Really?

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.800
Yes. That's why I'm asking how you know it.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.130
I-It's...

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:51.260
My grandma heard it when she was evacuated
to the countryside as a little girl.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.260
When she was evacuated?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.960
<i>That was a really long time ago.</i>

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.640
<i>Was it back when Gramps was a street
musician and used to travel all over?</i>

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.890
Sometimes, memories of that time
come flooding back to my grandma...

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.150
but she says they have no sound.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.160
She aches to hear that sound again.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:13.370
She says I must find that strange,
because they weren't good times.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:18.880
Her saying that makes me want
to hear the sound, too.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.880
But I've played all kinds of songs to
her and she says it's none of them.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.290
I started the Shamisen Appreciation Club

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.640
because I thought I might meet
someone who knows that song.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:36.440
<i>An impromptu piece changes
every time it's played.</i>

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:41.150
<i>Gramps spent thirty years
perfecting that piece.</i>

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.590
<i>Even if it was Gramps' sound she heard,</i>

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:47.150
<i>it'd be completely different
from the sound I know.</i>

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:51.160
<i>If that's the case... What form did it take?</i>

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.240
Hey! What're you doing to Shuri?!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:00.920
Shuri hates guys, you hear?!
Don't go making moves on her!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.360
Oh! Yui-chan!

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.060
It seems Sawamura-kun might know that song!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:06.620
What?

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.380
It sounds like you've got the
wrong idea. I'm done here.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.090
Huh?

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.480
<i>If her grandma can't remember it anymore,</i>

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.810
<i>there's no way for me to
find out about that sound.</i>

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.350
No! Don't go!

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.640
<i>Ooh, this is getting interesting!</i>

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.430
What's going on here, Shuri?!
You're not like this when I

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:26.860
Stop interfering and get lost!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.660
You should probably go.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:33.610
I-I... answered your question.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.740
Now you have to answer mine, Sawamura-kun.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.700
Will I ever be able to play that song?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.700
Or... can you play it, Sawamura-kun?

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.340
It's impossible.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.330
If it's the song I think it is, no one can play it.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.220
You should give up on it.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:04.070
Then, why?! Why did you tell her you knew it?!

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:08.030
How do you think Shuri's felt all this time?

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.570
I'm joining the Tsugaru
Shamisen Appreciation Club.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.410
What?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:16.130
I'm joining! And this guy's joining with me!

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.240
That okay with you?

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.450
And that's enough of that.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.200
I think I get the gist of what's going on.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.210
Since you have more members now,

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.820
let's make that shamisen
I'm holding onto usable.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.210
Usable?

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:34.320
Well, you see, I looked up the owner
of that shamisen, Ogata Kousuke.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.170
And I was shocked!

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:40.480
He's a household name in the shamisen world.
He's the prince of Tsugaru shamisen!

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:44.600
He goes by the name Kamiki
Seiryuu now, and he's <i>so</i> handsome!

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.270
Wh-Which is why...

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:54.030
we should all go to his performance tomorrow
night and get his permission to use it.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.030
Aomori

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.040
The Tanuma Household

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.610
There's no muddiness in your sound at all.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.690
It's like breathing the mountain air.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:30.880
Kousuke, I have nothing left to teach you.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.900
Just you coming here once a year

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.070
and showing me how much you've
improved makes me happy.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:41.150
Not at all. It's an honor.

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.290
Thank you for listening.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.690
First place in the A division at Hirosaki...

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.060
Winning the Nitabou Award in Kanagi...

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.460
Congratulations.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:53.210
Next year, our Souichi will be winning those.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.220
I won't let him.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.090
Tsugaru Shamisen School

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.090
Head of School Kamiki Ryuugen

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:59.220
Kamiki School

00:10:59.090 --> 00:10:59.220
Tsugaru Shamisen School

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:02.470
I'm back!

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:04.600
Is Kousuke still here?

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:07.520
Hey. I was just about to leave.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.800
What? You could stay a little longer.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.310
Don't you wanna catch my brother?

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.790
I've got to go. I have a live show
in Tokyo tomorrow night.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:16.770
Tokyo?

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.310
That's where Sawamura Setsu ran off to.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.410
Why are you so obsessed with that guy?

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.800
It's not <i>me</i> who's obsessed! It's my dad!

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:29.080
He's obsessed with the talent he
inherited. I keep telling you that.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.910
Yeah, yeah. That's been your
answer since forever ago.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.160
"The grandson of the master,
Sawamura Matsugoro."

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.720
"The boy with no interest in competing," right?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.930
But no one's heard him play.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.800
I once heard him play when I went
all the way to the front of his house.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:49.930
He was only in elementary school at the time,
but he was so skilled, it was scary.

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:55.320
It scared you, and you
still try to drag him out?

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.980
Well, I mean... He's just so good. It's not fair.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:04.590
If he's motivated by something other than
recognition or wanting people to listen,

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:05.780
that's fine, too, isn't it?

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.160
Besides...

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:13.660
If someone plays a sound you don't
have inside yourself, it electrifies you,

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.550
but it also fills you with jealousy.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:19.130
That sensation is so painful, so ugly...

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.050
It's a terrible thing.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.850
Aw, man. I didn't make it
all the way back home.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.310
Now my routine is disrupted.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.670
She's late.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.470
What's that teacher doing?

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:41.530
What about you?
Why are you coming along?

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:42.440
Shut up.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.800
<i>Kamiki Seiryuu.</i>

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.330
<i>He's the guy who won the competition
Wakana-chan entered, isn't it?</i>

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:50.950
I'm so sorry, guys!

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.930
The school day just <i>refused</i> to end!

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.230
What's with those clothes?!

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.690
It's getting dolled up that
took you so long, isn't it?

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.080
This is how I always dress.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:04.140
Liar!

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:14.030
Doesn't it seem like there are
a lot more girls here than guys?

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.490
Well, he <i>is</i> a heart-throb, after all.

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:19.610
The tickets were all sold out.
I had to beg them to do me a favor.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:29.370
Um... Sawamura-kun...

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:34.380
You said playing that song was
impossible yesterday. How come?

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.420
It's a very difficult piece.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:40.380
Technique-wise, it's impossible
for a beginner like you.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.300
And for you, Sawamura-kun?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.550
It's even more impossible.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:48.090
And what's more,
my emotions would get in the way.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.340
I wouldn't be able to play it
all the way to the end.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:54.350
<i>His emotions would get in the way?</i>

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.200
<i>Is he an idiot?</i>

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.890
<i>If he'd just try to play it, that'd be enough.</i>

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.110
<i>It's dark.</i>

00:15:22.280 --> 00:15:24.150
<i>In the middle of the empty darkness...</i>

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.520
<i>the sound of a bell...</i>

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:29.130
<i>...rings out.</i>

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.030
<i>It's sort of...</i>

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:37.540
<i>...frightening.</i>

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:01.320
<i>The sound...</i>

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:02.850
<i>...is wailing.</i>

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.650
<i>Sobbing, crying, ringing out.</i>

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:27.260
<i>I'm being pulled in...</i>

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.010
<i>to a world of nothingness.</i>

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.190
Good evening, everyone.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.490
I am Kamiki Seiryuu.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:06.680
He's so cool!

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.130
I'm amazed.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:14.490
I didn't know it was possible to get
such clear sounds out of a futozao.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.720
Dressing Room
Kamiki Seiryuu-sama

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:21.740
Honestly, that was just the best!
A wonderful performance!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:24.970
Oh! I'm a teacher, by the way. Koyabu Keiko.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.400
Oh, you must be the woman from
Umezono Academy who contacted me.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.110
You said you needed something?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:32.900
That's right!

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:33.860
Go ahead, Maeda-san.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.610
Uh... U-U-Um... I...

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:42.680
I run the Tsugaru Shamisen
Appreciation Club. My name is Maeda.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:45.130
I found this in the music prep room.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.910
Oh.

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.100
This brings back memories.
It's definitely mine.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.750
I was hoping you might let
us use it, if that's all right.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.430
Of course.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:58.010
That's why I left it there.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.930
Red sandalwood with beautiful grain.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.750
Metal-lined, double-reinforced joins.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.830
Double zigzags carved
inside for better sound.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.760
Why leave behind something so valuable?

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:14.160
I knew I wouldn't use it again.
So I left it for the next person.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.100
Even though it might've gotten thrown out?

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:19.060
If that happened, it happened.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:22.120
But I hoped it would be found by
someone who recognized its value.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:24.840
I don't get it.

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:27.410
That's fine with me.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.270
H-Hold on...

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.460
The atmosphere's getting
bad in here, Sawamura.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.720
The air's bad everywhere in Tokyo.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:35.100
That's not what I meant.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:37.470
Sawamura? Hey, what's your first name?

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.680
Ah, this is Sawamura Setsu-kun.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.520
<i>Sawamura... Setsu.</i>

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:48.970
<i>Surely this guy isn't Master
Sawamura Matsugoro's...</i>

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.790
Sensei.

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.230
Y-Yes?

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.290
This is a rare opportunity.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.900
Allow me to test the skills
of your club members.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.150
S-Skills?

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:03.500
Try playing something.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:05.510
Go on.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.830
Why'd he pick Sawamura?

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:18.140
Now that I think about it,
I haven't heard him play yet.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.900
<i>I'm the only one who knows!</i>

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:27.160
<i>Oh, I can't take it! It was fun being the only
one who knew, and here comes the payoff!</i>

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:30.640
<i>Now, show them how insanely
good you are at the shamisen!</i>

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.390
<i>This sounds really good,
like I thought it would.</i>

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:46.950
Wow.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.880
Oh, my, he's very good!

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:56.710
<i>Huh?</i>

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:05.920
<i>What kind of piece was "Jongara Bushi" again?</i>

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:11.400
<i>"Jongara Bushi"...</i>

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.160
<i>What kind of...</i>

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.420
<i>What was it?</i>

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.470
That's enough.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:42.470
More than enough.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.820
Yes, that was very nice.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.740
You're pretty good.

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.040
You played really well.

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:55.340
I was so surprised!

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:59.240
<i>Wait... What was with that boring performance?</i>

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:04.080
You have some skill, but it isn't
enough to just strike away recklessly.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:08.080
Still, for a first-year in
high school, it wasn't bad.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:10.840
Sawamura-kun?

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:11.590
Sawamura!

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:12.280
Sawamura-kun!

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.540
I'll go after him.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:15.640
What? Yui-chan?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:17.500
I-I'm so sorry about my student.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.000
Not at all. Please don't let it bother you.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.060
<i>Playing such insipid sounds
on my beautiful Kiyora 2...</i>

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:29.430
Hey! Hold it, will you?

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.250
Why didn't you play properly?

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:35.180
I've seen you play live before.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.280
I had zero interest in the shamisen,

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.580
but I was blown away.

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:46.700
You're so much better than that. You slacked off.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:48.410
And in front of a professional!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.530
Who do you think you are?

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:55.240
I didn't slack off.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:56.500
What?

00:21:57.030 --> 00:21:58.720
It shocked me, too.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:02.330
I couldn't play. I just couldn't play.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.630
What do I want Kamiki Seiryuu to hear?

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:07.080
For what purpose?

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:10.280
If I don't know those things, I can't play.

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:15.280
Even with Maeda-san...
When I see how desperate she is...

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.760
But even if I played it for her,
what would it achieve?

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.490
It's a different piece.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:25.120
How can I tell her I'll play it
for her when I feel this way?

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:28.110
Tanukichi

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:28.110
Diner

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:30.000
It's pouring!

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:33.020
We haven't had any custom

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:33.530
Restaurant

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:38.410
Setsu-san?

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:41.480
You shouldn't wander about
when it's pelting down like this!

00:22:41.480 --> 00:22:42.510
Hurry up and get insideвЂ”

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:43.790
Sakura-chan...

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.420
You're very kind.

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:46.310
Huh?

00:22:46.620 --> 00:22:52.810
If someone asked you to do something that
was impossible for you, what would you do?

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:56.120
I wouldn't do it.

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.970
Oh! But it depends on the situation.

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:01.640
If it was something really important...

00:23:01.640 --> 00:23:03.740
Something I'd regret if I didn't do it...

00:23:04.640 --> 00:23:07.240
I'd give it my best shot on my
own terms, even if I knew I'd fail.

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:10.970
Thank you.

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:22.200
<i>в™« Sakura... Sakura... в™« </i>

00:23:22.670 --> 00:23:27.890
<i>в™« The spring skies... в™« </i>

00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:31.260
I messed up again.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:33.410
Your posture's terrible.

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:35.130
Oh, it's you, Sawamura-kun.

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:36.690
You scared me.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:39.930
Raise the neck and bring your thumb
forward on the bachi, the pick.

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:41.770
R-Right.

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:47.690
You know, about that song you
want your grandma to hear...

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:51.650
It might be different from
the one she remembers...

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:53.200
Would that still be okay?

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:55.530
What?

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:00.720
Of course it's fine if it's different.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:05.210
Then, I'll play it.

00:24:06.620 --> 00:24:09.000
<i>Hey, Grandma...</i>

00:24:11.540 --> 00:24:14.380
<i>All those silent memories you have...</i>

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:18.840
I want to play for your grandma in person.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:23.620
<i>We're going to bring sound to them.</i>
